}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li720\loch\af1\dbch\f1\fs28\cf2\lang1033\li1 {\b\dbch\af1\loch\f1\fs48 Classes}{\dbch\af1\loch\f1\fs48  are constructs that define objects of the same type. A Java class uses variables to define data fields and methods to define behaviors. Additionally, a class provides a special type of methods, known as constructors, which are invoked to construct objects from the class.\par 
